  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "hA6UB9qH2AMlpxHuhHOInXlwEtM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:35:02.676Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "A document model is a schema plus reducers. Nothing in it names a database, a transport, a DOM, or a credential. That absence is deliberate, and it is what lets one package run in a browser and on a headless server with no per-host variant.\n\n## Where the difference lives instead\n\nEverything environment-specific is the host's, not the model's:\n\n- **Connect** renders the model's editor components and signs actions with the user's identity. It supplies the DOM, the modals, the drive browser.\n- **Switchboard** exposes the same documents over GraphQL and MCP so agents, back-ends, and integrations reach them without a browser, and it runs processors server-side.\n\nBoth embed a Reactor. Both feed the same reducers. The model, as the Academy puts it, \"doesn't know which host it's in, and it doesn't need to.\"\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThis is the practical payoff of keeping the Reactor a plain library rather than a service. Because the host owns the runtime, you get to choose the runtime \u2014 and you can have more than one at the same time. A finance ledger written once is simultaneously an offline-capable browser app and an API-addressable server resource, without a second implementation to keep in sync.\n\n## The mental model\n\nThink of the model as a cartridge and hosts as consoles. The cartridge carries logic and shape; the console supplies power, display, and controllers. Asking \"which host is this model for?\" is the wrong question \u2014 it is a category error, like asking which screen a function is for.\n\n## The design pressure it creates\n\nPortability only holds if you honour the boundary. A reducer that reaches for `window`, a wall clock, or a network call quietly binds the model to one runtime and breaks the property. That is the deeper reason reducers must be pure: purity is not fastidiousness, it is what keeps the cartridge playable on every console.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/02-architecture/02-host-applications.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:35:01.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:35:02.676Z"
    }
  },
